  {
    "request": "GET /api/quizzes",
    "status": 200,
    "type": "application/json",
    "json": [
      {
        "repository": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
        "repositoryName": "documents-fr",
        "id": "verb-plus-infinitive",
        "title": "Verbs followed by an infinitive",
        "text": "# Verbs followed by an infinitive\n\nThe learner is studying French and wants explanations in English.\n\nDrill a conjugated verb followed by an infinitive: the dictionary form of the next verb.\nCover direct combinations (`aimer`, `adorer`, `vouloir`, `pouvoir`, `devoir`, `aller`),\nthen expressions with `de` (`avoir envie de`, `essayer de`, `oublier de`) and `à`\n(`commencer à`, `apprendre à`). Keep the same subject for both actions.\n\n## Exercise\n\nGive a short English sentence and ask for natural French. Invent varied everyday situations:\nfood, travel, work, study, hobbies, plans and chores. Use different subjects and verbs; do not\nrely on a show, its characters or its dialogue. Start with direct combinations in the present,\nthen mix in `de`, `à`, questions and negation as the learner improves. Keep vocabulary simple\nso the challenge is choosing and forming the verb construction.\n\n## Traps to look for\n\n- Conjugating both verbs: `je veux partir` — I want to leave. Here `veux` changes with the\n  subject; `partir` stays in the infinitive because it names the wanted action.\n- Copying English -ing: `j'aime cuisiner` — I like cooking. French uses the infinitive after\n  `aimer`, even when English uses -ing.\n- Treating English \"to\" as a fixed French word: `je peux venir` — I can come;\n  `j'essaie de comprendre` — I'm trying to understand; `j'apprends à conduire` — I'm learning\n  to drive. Learn each leading expression with its connector; English cannot predict it.\n- Negating the wrong action: `je ne veux pas partir` — I don't want to leave;\n  `je veux ne pas oublier` — I want not to forget. Position changes what is negated.\n\n## Examples of the style wanted\n\n- Nous devons acheter du pain. — We need to buy bread.\n- Tu as envie de regarder un film ? — Do you feel like watching a film?\n- Elle commence à apprendre le français. — She's starting to learn French.\n"
      }
    ]
